&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dead Air Project&lt;/strong&gt; is an archive of ghostbox recordings, EVP sessions, and anomalous audio experiments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The goal is not to prove or claim anything —&lt;br&gt;
but to &lt;strong&gt;document&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;archive&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;let the listener decide&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All audio is presented as transparently as possible:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;raw recordings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;enhanced references (clearly marked)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no hidden processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;no sensational framing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="methodology"&gt;Methodology&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sessions may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ghostbox radio sweep&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;controlled silence recordings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;environmental audio capture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each session documents:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>